From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:31:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_brcm: accept the flow accelerator's lookup opcode

The flow accelerator in front of switch port 8 of BCM5301x and BCM58xx
puts the result of its flow lookup in the prepended tag: opcode 2, with
its header check result in byte 2 and the source port in byte 3 as in
opcode 0. Every frame that misses its flow table reaches the CPU that
way once the accelerator is in the path, so the tagger dropped them all.

Accept opcode 2 in the prepended tag only.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_brcm.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_brcm.c
@@ -53,6 +53,12 @@
 /* Ingress and egress opcodes */
 #define BRCM_OPCODE_SHIFT	5
 #define BRCM_OPCODE_MASK	0x7
+/* Egress opcode of the flow accelerator in front of port 8 of BCM5301x
+ * and BCM58xx, in the prepended tag only: the result of its flow lookup.
+ * Byte 2 then holds its header check result instead of a reason code;
+ * byte 3 holds the source port as with opcode 0.
+ */
+#define BRCM_OPCODE_FA_LOOKUP	0x2
 
 /* Ingress fields */
 /* 1st byte in the tag */
@@ -150,21 +156,26 @@
 {
 	int source_port;
 	u8 *brcm_tag;
+	u8 opcode;
 
 	if (unlikely(!pskb_may_pull(skb, BRCM_TAG_LEN)))
 		return NULL;
 
 	brcm_tag = skb->data - offset;
+	opcode = (brcm_tag[0] >> BRCM_OPCODE_SHIFT) & BRCM_OPCODE_MASK;
 
-	/* The opcode should never be different than 0b000 */
-	if (unlikely((brcm_tag[0] >> BRCM_OPCODE_SHIFT) & BRCM_OPCODE_MASK))
-		return NULL;
-
-	/* We should never see a reserved reason code without knowing how to
-	 * handle it
-	 */
-	if (unlikely(brcm_tag[2] & BRCM_EG_RC_RSVD))
+	if (likely(!opcode)) {
+		/* We should never see a reserved reason code without knowing
+		 * how to handle it
+		 */
+		if (unlikely(brcm_tag[2] & BRCM_EG_RC_RSVD))
+			return NULL;
+	} else if (opcode != BRCM_OPCODE_FA_LOOKUP || offset != ETH_HLEN) {
+		/* Any other opcode, or the flow accelerator's one outside
+		 * the prepended tag, is unexpected
+		 */
 		return NULL;
+	}
 
 	/* Locate which port this is coming from */
 	source_port = brcm_tag[3] & BRCM_EG_PID_MASK;
